Whisper: label the clipboard write's source and carry the replaced selection

What: carries, from the content process to the parent, a one-byte "who wrote this" label
(mozilla::ClipguardSource) and -- for a copy where a page copy/cut handler replaced the
person's selection -- the plain text the person had selected (capped at 4096). Both ride on
nsITransferable and as fields of IPCTransferable, not as clipboard flavors, so neither
reaches the native clipboard. nsCopySupport sets the label for the person's own Ctrl+C, a
page handler that replaced the data, or a script's execCommand (including copying a hidden
textarea); dom/events/Clipboard.cpp labels navigator.clipboard writes as AsyncClipboard. A
one-line Document getter exposes whether a page script's execCommand is running.
Why: the parent must tell the person's own copy (never blocked) from a script's write, and
for a handler that replaced the selection it must tell a real substitution (the replacement
is more dangerous than what the person selected) from a harmless one (a tidy-up, or a
"Read more at <url>" appended).
---
--- a/dom/base/Document.h
+++ b/dom/base/Document.h
@@ -4087,6 +4087,11 @@
